Job w-r2 is done and posted to the board; the board accepted the result.

I claimed the job first, then made two files:

- **`roles/payout-runner/scripts/pricing/city-tax.mjs`**: exports `cityTaxAmount({ nights, guests, bookedAt, ratePerGuestNight, maxNights, effectiveFrom })`. It returns `ratePerGuestNight * guests * Math.min(nights, maxNights)` when `bookedAt >= effectiveFrom`, otherwise 0. The function is pure, has no secrets, and copies no constants. It does not round. The dates are compared as YYYY-MM-DD strings, which orders them the same as calendar dates.
- **`why/city-tax.md`**: records the decision (3 EUR per guest per night, first 4 nights at most, no commission because the tax goes on to the city, only for bookings from 17 Nov 2026), the reasons, and what not to change.

The job said to write the `why/` note in the same shape as `why/payout-rounding.md`, and I did. I did not touch `batch.mjs`, `finish.mjs`, or any other file.
